{"name":"Thunder Bay","hex":"#cbd9d7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Thunder Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large bay of Thunder Bay district, Northwestern Ontario, Northern Ontario, Ontario, Canada, on Lake Superior, Great Lakes, North America.","A city in Thunder Bay district, Northwestern Ontario, Northern Ontario, Ontario, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Thunder_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thunder Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Thunder Bay is a city in and the seat of Thunder Bay District, Ontario, Canada. It is the most populous municipality in Northwestern Ontario and the second most populous municipality in Northern Ontario. Its population is 108,843 according to the 2021 Canadian census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Thunder_Bay_skyline.JPG/330px-Thunder_Bay_skyline.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder_Bay"},{"title":"Thunder","blocks":[{"text":"Thunder is the sound caused by lightning. Depending upon the distance from and nature of the lightning, it can range from a long, low rumble to a sudden, loud crack. The sudden increase in temperature and hence pressure caused by the lightning produces rapid expansion of the air in the path of a lightning bolt. In turn, this expansion of air creates a sonic shock wave, often referred to as a \"thunderclap\" or \"peal of thunder\". The scientific study of thunder is known as brontology and the irrational fear (phobia) of thunder is called brontophobia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Lakehead_University_Summer_Campus.jpg/500px-Lakehead_University_Summer_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Lakehead_University_Summer_Campus.jpg/500px-Lakehead_University_Summer_Campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALakehead_University_Summer_Campus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/MAgnust_Theatre_Thunder_Bay_October_One.jpg/500px-MAgnust_Theatre_Thunder_Bay_October_One.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/MAgnust_Theatre_Thunder_Bay_October_One.jpg/500px-MAgnust_Theatre_Thunder_Bay_October_One.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont